            <ArticleTitle>[Combined surgical treatment for bullous keratopathy with concomitant uncompensated glaucoma].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>64-67</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.17116/oftalma2015131264-67</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The article discusses a clinical case of combined surgical treatment for painful bullous keratopathy in an eye with uncompensated far-advanced glaucoma. Ex-PRESS Glaucoma Filtration Device was used for anterior chamber drainage. The procedure was supplemented by amniotic membrane implantation under the scleral flap, microdiathermocoagulation of large corneal epithelial bullae, and epikeratoplasty.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
